    <!-- the six-step walkthrough -->
    <string name="walk_step">Step %1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="walk_next">Next</string>
    <string name="walk_done">Start sketching</string>
    <string name="walk_skip">Skip</string>
    <string name="walk_t1">Draw one stroke</string>
    <string name="walk_b1">With no guide active, your first stroke is not a curve — it is extruded along the direction you are looking in and becomes a translucent 3D guide. Draw one now.</string>
    <string name="walk_t2">Orbit and look at it</string>
    <string name="walk_b2">Drag with two fingers to orbit — one finger is busy drawing. Pinch to zoom, three fingers to pan. The guide has depth: the orange edge marks where your first stroke was.</string>
    <string name="walk_b2_pen">Drag with one finger to orbit. The guide has depth: the orange edge marks where your first stroke was.</string>
    <string name="walk_t3">Draw on the guide</string>
    <string name="walk_b3">Every stroke from here projects onto that surface, so it picks up real 3D coordinates. That is the whole trick.</string>
    <string name="walk_t4">Bend it</string>
    <string name="walk_b4">Orbit to a new viewpoint, hit Bend, and draw a path. The first stroke keeps its shape and gets swept along what you just drew — a circle plus a big top-view circle gives you a doughnut.</string>
    <string name="walk_t5">Navigate</string>
    <string name="walk_b5">Double-tap snaps to the nearest of the six straight-on views, and a three-finger double-tap flips to orthographic. Press and hold to pin the orbit point; hold on empty space to reset. Change the lens from the menu.</string>
    <string name="walk_t6">The guide is also a mask</string>
    <string name="walk_b6">Anything hidden behind the guide cannot be erased or selected — cover what you want to protect, then erase freely. Toggle it under Isolate.</string>

